# GaAs, zincblende, conventional (non-primitive) cubic cell: 4 Ga + 4 As,
# a = 5.6533 Ang (the real, textbook experimental GaAs lattice constant).
#
# This is the HOST lattice of the whole example. --sublattice Ga picks the
# cation sites as the alloy sublattice; --species-b In turns it into the
# size-mismatched Ga(1-x)In(x)As alloy (GaAs and InAs differ by ~7% in lattice
# constant), --species-b Al into the nearly lattice-matched Ga(1-x)Al(x)As
# (~0.1%). The Ga sublattice is FCC -- geometrically frustrated for the
# pair-cluster enumeration stb-gqca does: no 2-coloring of an FCC lattice makes
# every nearest-neighbor pair unlike (README section 1.4).
SystemName GaAs zincblende (conventional cubic cell)
SystemLabel siesta

LatticeConstant 5.6533 Ang
%block LatticeVectors
  1.0000000000   0.0000000000   0.0000000000
  0.0000000000   1.0000000000   0.0000000000
  0.0000000000   0.0000000000   1.0000000000
%endblock LatticeVectors

NumberOfSpecies 2
%block ChemicalSpeciesLabel
 1  31  Ga
 2  33  As
%endblock ChemicalSpeciesLabel

NumberOfAtoms 8
AtomicCoordinatesFormat Fractional
%block AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
 0.00 0.00 0.00  1
 0.00 0.50 0.50  1
 0.50 0.00 0.50  1
 0.50 0.50 0.00  1
 0.25 0.25 0.25  2
 0.25 0.75 0.75  2
 0.75 0.25 0.75  2
 0.75 0.75 0.25  2
%endblock AtomicCoordinatesAndAtomicSpecies
